## Getting Started

### Option A — Run Locally

**Prerequisites:** Python 3.9 or higher

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/yourusername/ag-rag-system.git
cd ag-rag-system

# Create and activate virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # Mac/Linux
venv\Scripts\activate     # Windows

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run the app
streamlit run app.py
```

Open your browser at `http://localhost:8501`

Enter your API keys in the sidebar and start asking questions.

### Option B — Use the Colab Notebook

1. Open `ag_rag_system.ipynb` in Google Colab
2. Add your API keys to Colab Secrets (key icon in left sidebar)
3. Run cells in order from top to bottom
4. Use Cell 8 to test queries interactively
5. Run Cell 9 + Final Cell to export and push to GitHub for deployment

---

## Deploying to Streamlit Community Cloud

1. Fork or push this repository to your GitHub account
2. Go to [share.streamlit.io](https://share.streamlit.io)
3. Sign in with GitHub
4. Click **New app**
5. Select your repository and set main file path to `app.py`
6. Click **Deploy**

Your app will be live at `https://yourappname.streamlit.app`

**For production deployment** — add your API keys as Streamlit Secrets rather than entering them via the sidebar UI. In your Streamlit Cloud dashboard go to App settings → Secrets and add:

```toml
GROQ_API_KEY = "your_groq_key"
LANGCHAIN_API_KEY = "your_langsmith_key"
```

Then update `app.py` to load from Streamlit secrets:

```python
groq_key = st.secrets["GROQ_API_KEY"]
langsmith_key = st.secrets["LANGCHAIN_API_KEY"]
```

---

## API Keys Required

| Key | Where to Get It | Cost |
|---|---|---|
| `GROQ_API_KEY` | [console.groq.com](https://console.groq.com) | Free — no credit card |
| `LANGCHAIN_API_KEY` | [smith.langchain.com](https://smith.langchain.com) | Free tier — 5,000 traces/month |

DuckDuckGo search requires no API key.

